1|0@electronic_cigarette^1440408008#cudq7wc:arealbabyturtle$:I'm going to be frank with you because if you're serious and not a troll than you need some more information. The battery of something like the rdna40 is more than capable of powering something like a atlantis and since they both use the now standardized 510 threading it would be perfectly safe since everything is compatable. Unfortunatley the only time an atomizer can short out and create a dangerous situation is when somebody creates a short either using the same atlantis on a mechanical mod with a hybrid top cap, or using batteries within a mod that do not have a high enough amp rating. To be honest I would bring this up to the owner of the shop and if the shop owner validates the employees claim then find a new shop because they are unqualified to run it. Any shop that gives out false information should be shut down especialy considering how delicate the market is. In a new market we have to be accurate otherwise stringint regulation will be put in place to protect those unwilling to do their own independent research and blindly listening to someone they consider an authority on the subject. /rant over 
